From 68a4dfe2ace0bcf7cd49373160e4fa8f9d5cf0d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:35:37 -0400
Subject: Inherit the compositor-wide DPMS state when a monitor connects

Bug: CMonitor::onConnect() brings every new monitor up enabled (m_dpmsStatus defaults to
true and the output is committed with setEnabled(true) before applyMonitorRule()), without
consulting g_pCompositor->m_dpmsStateOn. Many panels drop HPD a few seconds after losing
signal and reconnect shortly after (input auto-scan; see hyprwm/Hyprland#5557). With DPMS
off that hotplug destroys and re-creates the CMonitor, and the new one is modeset and lit:
"dpms off" lasts about 8 seconds and the desktop comes back on with nobody at the keyboard.
On this machine (amdgpu, HP 22cwa on HDMI-A-1 and a bus-powered MSI MP161 on USB-C DP Alt
Mode, DP-2) hypridle's journal shows one wl_output removed/re-added pair per panel at +6.3 s
and +8.4 s after every DPMS-off, and the compositor log shows a fresh "Modesetting" for each.
Confirmed by eye 2026-09-13 with a 15 s idle timeout: dark at 15 s, lit again at ~23 s.
Each re-creation is also a cold DisplayPort link training of the bus-powered panel, which is
what intermittently trains into a marginal, visibly jittering link (Fault C in
docs/agent-runbooks/display-output-instability.md) - observed the same day at 10:14:15
with no suspend involved.

Fix: in the new-monitor path of onConnect(), set m_dpmsStatus from
g_pCompositor->m_dpmsStateOn and commit the output with that enabled-state. When DPMS is
globally off the monitor is still registered (wl_output, workspaces, layout, mode recorded by
applyMonitorRule() - whose commit is then a harmless disable commit) but not lit and not
link-trained. Every existing DPMS-on path (the dpms dispatcher, misc:mouse_move_enables_dpms,
misc:key_press_enables_dpms, wlr-output-power) goes through setDPMS(true), which enables a
monitor whose m_dpmsStatus is false exactly as it does for any other DPMS-off monitor. While
DPMS is on (the default, and at startup) behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream: unfixed on main as of 2026-09-13 (onConnect still enables unconditionally);
#5557 and #8377 were closed in the move to discussions, not fixed. PR draft in
upstream-pr.md next to this file.

Retires when: an Arch hyprland release whose CMonitor::onConnect() honours the compositor
DPMS state on connect. Packaged locally as 0.56.2-3.1; any Arch pkgrel or pkgver bump
outranks it automatically (the pacman hook then says whether to rebase or retire).

diff -ruN a/src/output/Monitor.cpp b/src/output/Monitor.cpp

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

